## Wait for Compute Nodes

Wait for all compute nodes to become accessible via SSH, for up to
`node_boot_timeout` seconds. A node that is not reachable by then is not slow,
it has failed to provision, and the checks below cannot tell you anything
useful about it.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Wait for compute nodes to be accessible -->
```bash
deadline=$(( SECONDS + ${node_boot_timeout:-600} ))
while true ; do
	pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" true \
		>/dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "compute nodes: OK"; break; }
	if (( SECONDS >= deadline )); then
		echo "compute nodes: FAILED, no SSH in ${node_boot_timeout:-600}s"
		echo "Check the node console, and the cloud-init server with"
		echo "  podman logs cloud-init-server"
		exit 1
	fi
	echo "Waiting for compute nodes..."
	sleep 10
done
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

`sshd` answers before cloud-init has finished: its final stage still has to
write the munge key and run the `runcmd` restarts. Wait for it to complete on
every node, so that the resource manager steps below do not restart daemons
that cloud-init is restarting at the same time.

`cloud-init status --wait` blocks for as long as cloud-init takes, with no
limit of its own, so bound it on the node with `cloud_init_timeout`. The test
on the exit status fails this step when cloud-init timed out (`timeout` reports
124) or failed (1), and lets a run that finished with recoverable errors (2)
through: any `cc_*` module warning produces one, and a cluster whose nodes are
up and usable should not stop here for that. `$?` and `$rc` are escaped so that
the compute node expands them rather than the head node.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Wait for cloud-init to finish on the compute nodes -->
```bash
pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" \
	"timeout ${cloud_init_timeout:-600} cloud-init status --wait; \
	rc=\$?; [ \$rc -eq 0 ] || [ \$rc -eq 2 ]" \
	|| { echo "cloud-init: FAILED or did not finish in time"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

If IPoIB is configured, check that it came up on every compute: NetworkManager
activates each node's connection once the interface and its InfiniBand link
appear.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify IPoIB on the compute nodes -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ipoib -->
```bash
for ((t=0; ; t++)) ; do
	pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" \
		"nmcli -g GENERAL.STATE connection show ${ipoib_dev} | grep -qx activated" \
		>/dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "compute IPoIB: OK"; break; }
	(( t < 30 )) || { echo "compute IPoIB: FAILED"; exit 1; }
	echo "Waiting for IPoIB on the compute nodes..."
	sleep 10
done
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
